@startuml
title Custom policy and standard LE Audio ownership

skinparam monochrome true
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
hide footbox

actor "Control application" as PolicyClient
participant "Custom policy service" as Policy
participant "OpenEarable Unicast Server" as Server
actor "LE Audio Unicast Client" as AudioClient

PolicyClient -> Policy: Set ACL policy or server QoS preferences
Policy --> PolicyClient: Correlated command result

AudioClient -> Server: Discover PACS
Server --> AudioClient: Published LC3 capabilities
AudioClient -> Server: ASCS Config Codec\n(selected supported LC3 configuration)
Server --> AudioClient: Codec Configured ASE\n(configured codec + server QoS preferences)
AudioClient -> AudioClient: Configure CIG/CIS in local controller
AudioClient -> Server: ASCS Config QoS\n(actual SDU interval, framing, PHY,\nMax SDU, RTN, latency, presentation delay)
Server --> AudioClient: QoS Configured ASE
AudioClient -> Server: ASCS Enable / Start

Server -> Policy: Publish effective ACL and\nstandard-negotiated stream state
Policy --> PolicyClient: runtime_state notification

note over PolicyClient,AudioClient
The custom service controls device-owned policy only.
PACS and ASCS remain authoritative for codec capabilities,
codec selection, actual CIS QoS, and stream lifecycle.
end note
@enduml
